preConditionHook:
// GUARD (2026-09-17): the prior session's existence is a bool set at the date
// change, never a test of the price against the xxxD -1 sentinel -- a
// back-adjusted series can print -1.00 as a real price. The EL twin sets the
// same flag on date <> date[1], so the two twins are now silent on the SAME
// bars (before this the twin answered from chart data on the first partial
// day). Mentions of the -1 SENTINEL below describe what the xxxD functions
// return, not how this rule guards them.
// The opening gap has NOT been filled early: over the last checkBars bars the
// lowest low has stayed above the prior session's close (long side), or the
// highest high below it (short). Brooks: a large gap that does not reverse
// early usually starts a strong trend day. checkBars = 12 is the miner's
// reading of 'early'.
//
// This is the atomic HOLD half only. The gap-SIZE half of the same source
// composite is SessionGapAtrMagnitude and is deliberately not folded in: the
// two are independently meaningful and the pane ANDs entry rules, so two
// placements beat one compound.
//
// prevClose IS CloseD(1), which the twin calls and the engine does not
// expose. MEASURED (the closed register row): the day is the wall-clock
// CALENDAR date, the same boundary as date <> date[1], and the function
// returns a -1 SENTINEL while fewer than that many complete days exist. The
// mirror is exact from its first observed date change on -- a day's close is
// the close of its LAST bar, and close[1] on the date-change bar is exactly
// that, so no running accumulator and no sawStart guard are needed as they
// are for HighD/LowD. Before that first observed change TradeStation answers
// from chart data the engine's window never showed it, so the mirror holds
// the -1 sentinel and is silent; the guard is load-bearing, since -1 as a
// price sits under every real price and would pass the long side outright.
//
// The window extremes mirror EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest() and
// Lowest() call: seeded at bar 0, scanning bars 1..Length-1, strict
// comparison, the window INCLUSIVE of the current bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE,
// so its comparison carries the 2.22e-12 tolerance -- el_gt / el_lt, as in
// Breakout (the reference).
//
// Not LowHoldsPriorClose, whose level is the PREVIOUS BAR's close and whose
// test is this bar's low alone. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    prevClose = close[1];
    havePrev = true;
}
loWin = low[0];
hiWin = high[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)checkBars; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], loWin)) loWin = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], hiWin)) hiWin = high[i];
}
holdUp = havePrev && el_gt(loWin, prevClose);
holdDn = havePrev && el_lt(hiWin, prevClose);
